   "ts_iso": "2025-12-24T19:43:21+00:00",
   "from_me": true,
   "sender_jid": null,
   "type": 0,
   "text": "Y preparamos esto\nCon uno de los findings\nPara ver de contribuir a research en Labs con IA \n\nY opensource open medicine",
   "starred": false
  },
  {
   "id": 1637746,
   "key_id": "3EB077D74712EDFBE470D1",
   "ts_ms": 1766605409000,
   "ts_iso": "2025-12-24T19:43:29+00:00",
   "from_me": true,
   "sender_jid": null,
   "type": 0,
   "text": "https://github.com/IvanWeissVanDerPol/HIV-Research",
   "starred": false
  },
  {
   "id": 1637747,
   "key_id": "3EB04F9A0365174649E076",
   "ts_ms": 1766605413000,
   "ts_iso": "2025-12-24T19:43:33+00:00",
   "from_me": true,
   "sender_jid": null,
   "type": 0,
   "text": "The p-adic framework treats biological sequences not as linear strings but as hierarchical structures that can be mapped to hyperbolic space. This approach reveals hidden patterns in viral evolution that are invisible to traditional sequence alignment methods.\n\nP-adic geometry identifies HIV sentinel glycans (N58, N103, N204) whose removal optimally exposes bnAb epitopes - corroborated by AlphaFold3 showing inverse correlation (r=-0.89) between Goldilocks score and structural stability.",
   "starred": false
  },
